WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
Let's explore some advanced features and optimization strategies that can help you improve

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.176
your campaign performance.

00:00:05.176 --> 00:00:09.120
After watching this video, you'll be able to enhance your campaigns

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.708
through several key features.

00:00:10.708 --> 00:00:14.280
You'll learn to apply rule-based bidding, implement scheduled

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:19.680
bid rules for specific timeframes, make bid adjustments for placements, leverage Amazon

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.280
built audiences for targeted bid boosts, and set up budget rules to manage campaign

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.129
spend effectively.

00:00:25.129 --> 00:00:29.800
In the advertising console, select a specific campaign within the campaign

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.680
manager, you can then apply advanced features on the campaign settings page or during campaign

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:35.066
creation.

00:00:35.066 --> 00:00:39.700
Let's begin with rule-based bidding, an automated strategy that reduces manual

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:45.320
bid adjustments, return on ad spend, or ROAS measures the revenue generated for every

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:47.040
dollar spent on advertising.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.480
Once you set your ROAS parameters, Amazon automatically

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:54.660
adjusts your bids, which can increase up to three times your base bid during high opportunity

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:54.984
periods.

00:00:54.984 --> 00:00:59.840
For example, you could set your ROAS to three as a guardrail within the campaign

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:00.265
settings.

00:01:00.265 --> 00:01:05.360
Now that you understand rule-based bidding, let's explore scheduled bid rules.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.880
This feature allows you to automatically increase bids for specific timeframes, helping you

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.068
focus on peak shopping hours and events.

00:01:12.068 --> 00:01:14.880
For example, you could apply a rule to automatically

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.668
increase your bids by 10 percent on Saturday evenings between 5 and 9 p.

00:01:18.668 --> 00:01:18.939
m.

00:01:18.939 --> 00:01:19.480
when you've

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:20.883
noticed higher conversion rates.

00:01:20.883 --> 00:01:24.040
Another way to refine your bidding strategy is through

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.341
adjusting bids by placement.

00:01:25.341 --> 00:01:28.920
This allows you to tailor your bids to help improve visibility

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.179
in high converting placements.

00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:33.640
You can increase bids for top-of-search placements and adjust

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:34.984
bids for product pages.

00:01:34.984 --> 00:01:38.680
For example, consider a 20 percent top-of-search bid adjustment

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.700
and monitor performance.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.440
To help further enhance your campaign performance, let's look at bid

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.423
boosting for Amazon-built audiences.

00:01:45.423 --> 00:01:48.200
This feature enhances your targeting with audience

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:48.811
bid adjustments.

00:01:48.811 --> 00:01:52.480
These adjustments apply to audiences such as those with a high likelihood

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:56.800
of purchase based on recent shopping activity, previous brand purchasers who bought your

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.960
product in the last three months, and brand product considers who clicked or added to

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:01.832
cart without purchasing.

00:02:01.832 --> 00:02:05.320
Consider starting with a 10 to 20 percent bid increase for these

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:09.800
audiences and measure results over two weeks before further adjustments.

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:14.335
Finally, let's explore budget rules for managing your campaign spend effectively.

00:02:14.335 --> 00:02:15.160
Schedule-based

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:20.000
budget rules allow you to automatically increase budgets for specific timeframes, particularly

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.440
useful during seasonal peaks and promotional periods.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.880
For example, you can set your budget

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.623
to increase by 30 percent for Black Friday.

00:02:27.623 --> 00:02:29.680
Performance-based rules help you capitalize

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.517
on well-performing campaigns by automatically adjusting budgets based on key metrics.

00:02:34.517 --> 00:02:34.920
These

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:40.320
metrics include advertising cost of sale, ACoS, which measures your ad spend relative

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:40.981
to sales.

00:02:40.981 --> 00:02:45.280
Click-through rate, which shows how often customers click your ads when they

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:49.320
see them, and conversion rate, which indicates how often customers purchase after clicking

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:50.080
your ads.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.500
These advanced features work together to optimize your campaigns.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.640
Start by testing

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.280
individual features on a few campaigns, monitor results for at least two weeks, and gradually

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.502
expand successful optimizations that align with your business objectives.

00:03:03.502 --> 00:03:04.440
Apply advanced

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.360
features in the advertising console.
